  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Burnham says he would put PR in Labour manifesto and scrap triple lock to fund social care – UK politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/29/andy-burnham-labour-conference-liverpool-speech-triple-lock-pension-angela-rayner-lucy-powell-bridget-phillipson-uk-politics-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>PM, in first speech to party conference as leader, insists his plans are a ‘good deal’ for older people</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/29/andy-burnham-labour-conference-pension-triple-lock-social-care\">Burnham to signal willingness to look at scrapping pension triple lock to fund social care</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Angela Rayner</strong>, the housing secretary, has apparently confirmed that Andy Burnham will float the prospect of getting rid of the pensions triple lock to help fund the creation of an NHS-style care service.</p><p>Asked about the prospect on Sky’s Electoral Dysfunction podcast, Rayner said that Burnham was “absolutely right to start the conversation” and that he was being “brave”.</p><p>The high principle on this is that people have paid in all their lives. They are willing, I think, to look at that.</p><p>What they don’t want is what they consider to be, quite frankly, incompetent politicians that are going to take something from us to fill a black hole.</p><p>When we met with Andy [Burnham] this week, it certainly wasn’t mentioned.</p><p>But I do think that it’s important that Labour make sure that working-class people know that they’re on their side, and this would be a direction of travel that would say the opposite to that.</p><p>What I understood the national care service to be was a universal benefit: everybody paid in and everybody gets out, and that is what actually the principle of that is.</p><p>Going to a group of people who are getting around £12,500 a year in order to pay for it to take away their security is wrong.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/29/andy-burnham-labour-conference-liverpool-speech-triple-lock-pension-angela-rayner-lucy-powell-bridget-phillipson-uk-politics-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T16:52:09"
    },
    {
      "title": "Prime Minister Andy Burnham Lays Out Plan to Change UK in Emotional Speech at Labour Conference",
